{
  "about": "Module frames and names as both apps draw them (web moduleLabels.ts, desktop rendering/ModuleLabels.cpp). Scene px at 8 px per stud; a name is charWidth x font px wide per character so fonts do not matter. A name is never longer than the module's edge it sits on (its parts, the frame less 4 px each end): it wraps to two lines, then shrinks (not under minFontPx), then is cut short with an ellipsis. A module with some parts on a hidden sheet frames only the parts that show, dashed with partlyHiddenFrameDash. Same file in both repos. Names are placed together (placement): each in turn takes the lowest-scoring place around its module (scores in moduleLabels.ts MODULE_NAME_SCORE), keeping clear of parts and other names, on the outside edge of a ring, never upside down (left reads bottom to top, rotation -90; right top to bottom, rotation 90); parts are scene rectangles in studs, compare positions within 0.01 px. Each module's default colour (colours) comes from its id (FNV-1a over UTF-16 code units, modulo the palette), stepping on through the palette when a neighbour within neighbourStuds has it.",
  "charWidth": 0.6,
  "minFontPx": 16,
  "style": {
    "frameStroke": "rgba(100,180,255,0.8)",
    "frameDash": [
      6,
      4
    ],
    "partlyHiddenFrameDash": [
      2,
      6
    ],
    "nameFill": "rgba(100,180,255,0.9)",
    "nameStroke": "rgba(0,0,0,0.6)",
    "nameFontStyle": "bold",
    "nameStrokeWidth": "max(2, fontPx / 12)",
    "nameLineHeight": 1,
    "customFrameAlpha": 0.8,
    "customNameAlpha": 0.9,
    "fullNameBackground": "rgba(0,0,0,0.75)",
    "fullNamePad": "round(fontPx / 4)"
  },
